brcm-dma.resource/BDMA_CheckJob                     brcm-dma.resource/BDMA_CheckJob

   NAME
	BDMA_CheckJob -- has the job been replied?

   SYNOPSIS
	done = BDMA_CheckJob( job )
	d0                    a0

	BOOL BDMA_CheckJob(struct BDMAJob *);

   FUNCTION
	As CheckIO() does for a request: TRUE when the job was replied to its port (or was never started), FALSE while it is in flight. It does not give the
	result and does not free anything: BDMA_WaitJob() does, or GetMsg() on the port.

   INPUTS
	job             a job

   RESULTS
	done            TRUE or FALSE

   SEE ALSO
	brcm-dma.resource/BDMA_WaitJob()

brcm-dma.resource/BDMA_CloseClient               brcm-dma.resource/BDMA_CloseClient

   NAME
	BDMA_CloseClient -- end a session

   SYNOPSIS
	BDMA_CloseClient( client )
	a0

	VOID BDMA_CloseClient(struct BDMAClient *);

   FUNCTION
	What is in flight is aborted, the jobs of the client are freed, and so is its port when the client made it. A job that is over but whose reply is
	still to come is waited for, a few milliseconds at most.

   INPUTS
	client          a client, or NULL

   NOTES
	The replies that wait on a port that is not the client's own are the program's to take (GetMsg(), BDMA_WaitJob()) before it closes. A task that
	leaves without closing its client leaves its jobs running: the DMA may then write into memory that was freed, as a device does with the
	IORequest of a task that is gone.

   SEE ALSO
	brcm-dma.resource/BDMA_OpenClientTagList()

brcm-dma.resource/BDMA_FreeJob                       brcm-dma.resource/BDMA_FreeJob

   NAME
	BDMA_FreeJob -- give a job back

   SYNOPSIS
	BDMA_FreeJob( job )
	a0

	VOID BDMA_FreeJob(struct BDMAJob *);

   FUNCTION
	A job that is in flight, or over whose reply has not come yet, is left alone: wait for it (BDMA_WaitJob()) or abort it first.

   INPUTS
	job             a job from BDMA_AllocJobTagList(), or NULL

   NOTES
	The reply of a job must have been taken off its port (BDMA_WaitJob(), GetMsg()) before the job is freed.

   SEE ALSO
	brcm-dma.resource/BDMA_AllocJobTagList()

brcm-dma.resource/BDMA_OpenClientTagList   brcm-dma.resource/BDMA_OpenClientTagList

   NAME
	BDMA_OpenClientTagList -- begin a session

   SYNOPSIS
	client = BDMA_OpenClientTagList( tagList )
	d0                               a0

	struct BDMAClient *BDMA_OpenClientTagList(CONST struct TagItem *);

   FUNCTION
	A client names the program for the tools, keeps the default reply port and priority of its jobs, and gives them back when it is closed. Without
	BDC_ReplyPort it makes a port of its own: that port belongs to the task that opens the client, which is the only one that can sleep in
	BDMA_WaitJob() for the jobs that use it.

   INPUTS
	tagList         BDC_Name         STRPTR, a name (copied, 31 characters at most)
	                BDC_ReplyPort    struct MsgPort *, the default reply port of the jobs: a signal port (PA_SIGNAL) for a task, a software interrupt
	                                 port (PA_SOFTINT) for an interrupt handler
	                BDC_Priority     ULONG, the default BDPRI_* of the jobs
	                BDJ_ErrorCode    ULONG *, receives BDERR_OK or the reason

   RESULTS
	client          a client, or NULL

   EXAMPLES
	client = BDMA_OpenClientTags(BDC_Name, "MyPlayer", TAG_DONE);

   NOTES
	A task context.

   SEE ALSO
	brcm-dma.resource/BDMA_CloseClient()

brcm-dma.resource/BDMA_OpenClientTags         brcm-dma.resource/BDMA_OpenClientTags

   NAME
	BDMA_OpenClientTags -- BDMA_OpenClientTagList() with the tags as arguments

