   FUNCTION
	The same as BDMA_QueryInfoTagList(); generated inline from the SFD, not a function of the resource.

brcm-dma.resource/BDMA_QueryJobTagList       brcm-dma.resource/BDMA_QueryJobTagList

   NAME
	BDMA_QueryJobTagList -- what a job says about itself

   SYNOPSIS
	answers = BDMA_QueryJobTagList( job, tagList )
	d0                              a0   a1

	ULONG BDMA_QueryJobTagList(struct BDMAJob *, CONST struct TagItem *);

   FUNCTION
	As GetDTAttrs() does: each tag names a value and the ULONG * that goes with it receives it. A tag that this version does not know is skipped and its
	place left alone.

   INPUTS
	job             a job
	tagList         BDJI_State       BDJS_QUEUED, BDJS_RUNNING, BDJS_DONE, BDJS_ABORTED, BDJS_FAILED or BDJS_IDLE (described, not started)
	                BDJI_Error       BDERR_*, once the job is over
	                BDJI_BytesDone   the bytes of the job once it is over (0 for a job that failed or was aborted)
	                BDJI_Timeout     the BDJ_Timeout that applies to the job, in microseconds, after the limits (0 or more than 10000000 gives 10000000)

   RESULTS
	answers         the number of values written

   SEE ALSO
	brcm-dma.resource/BDMA_WaitJob()

brcm-dma.resource/BDMA_QueryJobTags             brcm-dma.resource/BDMA_QueryJobTags

   NAME
	BDMA_QueryJobTags -- BDMA_QueryJobTagList() with the tags as arguments

   SYNOPSIS
	answers = BDMA_QueryJobTags( job, tag1Type, ... )
	d0                           a0   a1

	ULONG BDMA_QueryJobTags(struct BDMAJob *, ULONG, ...);

   FUNCTION
	The same as BDMA_QueryJobTagList(); generated inline from the SFD, not a function of the resource.

brcm-dma.resource/BDMA_RemRange                 brcm-dma.resource/BDMA_RemRange

   NAME
	BDMA_RemRange -- take back a range of memory (V0.2)

   SYNOPSIS
	error = BDMA_RemRange( range )
	d0                     a0

	LONG BDMA_RemRange(struct BDMARange *);

   FUNCTION
	Removes a range that BDMA_AddRangeTagList() declared, and frees it. Do it before the memory goes back to its owner (RELEASE_BUFFER of the
	firmware, for a framebuffer): from that moment no job of the client is accepted there.

	A job of the client that is in flight on the range (queued, running, or over with its reply not taken) is not interrupted: the call gives
	BDERR_BUSY and the range stays. Wait for the job (BDMA_WaitJob()) or abort it. The jobs of the client that were checked against the range and
	are not started are marked: BDMA_StartJob() replies them with BDERR_RANGE, until BDMA_SetJobTagList() checks them again.

   INPUTS
	range           a range of a client that is still open

   RESULTS
	error           BDERR_OK, BDERR_BUSY, or BDERR_ARGS for NULL

   NOTES
	A task context. Call it from the task that starts the jobs of the client: no job may be started on the range during the call.

   SEE ALSO
	brcm-dma.resource/BDMA_AddRangeTagList(), brcm-dma.resource/BDMA_CloseClient()

brcm-dma.resource/BDMA_ResetStatistics          brcm-dma.resource/BDMA_ResetStatistics

   NAME
	BDMA_ResetStatistics -- set the statistics back to zero

   SYNOPSIS
	BDMA_ResetStatistics()

	VOID BDMA_ResetStatistics(VOID);

   FUNCTION
	Sets to zero what BDMA_QueryInfoTagList() reports as measures: BDI_Jobs, BDI_MegaBytes, BDI_Failures, BDI_Aborts, BDI_Timeouts, BDI_Busy,
	BDI_Slices, BDI_Deferred, BDI_WaitMaxUs, BDI_BusyMs0, BDI_BusyMs1 and the sizes BDI_Size64 to BDI_SizeBig, BDI_IrqCalls, BDI_IrqMCycles and BDI_IrqKInstr. BDI_QueueMax starts again at the
	number of jobs waiting at that moment. The jobs in the queue and on the channels are not touched.

	The counters are shared by every client, and there is no check: whoever calls this resets them for all. It is meant for measuring (read, do
	something, read again), not for a program that wants its own counters: it subtracts two reads instead.

   NOTES
	Can be called from a task or an interrupt; it only briefly disables the interrupts.

   SEE ALSO
	brcm-dma.resource/BDMA_QueryInfoTagList()

brcm-dma.resource/BDMA_SetJobTagList           brcm-dma.resource/BDMA_SetJobTagList

   NAME
	BDMA_SetJobTagList -- change a job that is not in flight

   SYNOPSIS
	error = BDMA_SetJobTagList( job, tagList )
	d0                          a0   a1

	LONG BDMA_SetJobTagList(struct BDMAJob *, CONST struct TagItem *);

   FUNCTION
	The tags name what changes (an address, the length, the rows, a pitch, a priority), what they leave out stays; the job is checked again. The kind
	of the job does not change: a copy stays a copy, a fill a fill.

   INPUTS
	job             a job
	tagList         tags of BDMA_AllocJobTagList()

   RESULTS
	error           BDERR_OK; BDERR_BUSY if the job is in flight; the other reasons of BDMA_AllocJobTagList(), and then the job is as it was

   EXAMPLES
	BDMA_SetJobTags(job, BDJ_Src, nextFrame, TAG_DONE);
	BDMA_StartJob(job);

   SEE ALSO
	brcm-dma.resource/BDMA_AllocJobTagList(), brcm-dma.resource/BDMA_StartJob()

